<doctext field_name="doctext">Thanks to Autobox you can do
&lt;code&gt;
use autobox::universal qw(type);

say type("42");  # STRING
say type(42);    # INTEGER
say type(42.0);  # FLOAT 
say type(undef); # UNDEF 
&lt;/code&gt;
See chocolateboy's response in &lt;a href="http://stackoverflow.com/questions/12686335/how-to-tell-apart-numeric-scalars-and-string-scalars-in-perl"&gt;"How to tell apart numeric scalars and string scalars in Perl?" &lt;/a&gt;
</doctext>
